vaultquest notes -- braindump

k so the name is VaultQuest. basically making a discord eco bot but not a boring one where u just spam /work all day. i want some actual strategy. 

hosting n stuff
- probably gonna go with oracle cloud ARM for production since its free and has like 24gb ram lol. overkill but whatever. 
- dev on our own machines is fine. 
- MUST use a private github repo. i dont want to leak the token like a complete idiot. 

the stack
- nodejs + discord.js (standard)
- better-sqlite3. i hate async/await for simple math so sync is way better for balances n stuff. plus its fast.

gameplay bits
factions are a big thing. let people form gangs. 
- shared vaults: you pool money together. maybe 2% interest? but it makes the gang a target for mega heists. high risk high reward i guess. 
- taxes: factions can "claim" a channel. if someone runs /work there, the gang takes a 5% cut. ez money.

shops & stuff
don't just hold coins, that's boring. users buy "shops". 
- like a coffee shop costs 50k and makes 500/hr. 
- but people can sabotage you. pay 5k to shut a shop down for 6 hours. 
- unless u have a "security guard" item to block it. 

vault traps
this is the fun part. 
- shock wire: fail a heist = jailed for way longer.
- ink bombs: failure = name turns red for 24h. everyone will know ur a thief. 
- false bottom: they think they won but they get 0 coins lol. ultimate troll.

some code things to remember
- passive income: DONT use a loop. itll kill the cpu. just calculate it when they check. 
  `const profit = Math.floor((Date.now() - lastClaim) / 3600000) * hourlyRate;`
- heist math: put it in math.js. 
  ```javascript
  const calculateSuccess = (attackerPower, defenderSecurity) => {
      let chance = 0.40; // base 40%
      chance += (attackerPower * 0.1);
      chance -= (defenderSecurity * 0.05);
      return Math.random() < chance;
  };
  ```
- TRANSACTIONS: always use them for money. if it crashes mid-transfer we're screwed. 

ui/ux
buttons and menus only. typing commands is so 2018. 
- for /shop, use a select menu. then interaction.update() with a "confirm" button. 

